  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As some might've noticed, in the beta, the \"Code\" filter is gone from the camera filters. However, this decision has left a handful of users displeased, as it was a very unique filter with several niche use-cases.\nMost people who utilize the filter on the other hand, are just looking for a way to visualize the map where it's normally too dark to see or if there are transparent/invisible meshes. A substitute for this \"Code\" filter would be to add one or more debug filters, which would functionally do the same thing, rendering the world with a special shader.\nSo here are two filter proposals:\nNormal filter.\nWireframe filter.\nThese filters would be incredibly handy for both world and avatar creators alike, letting them easily inspect their models and find issues on them in a runtime environment. Not only would this allow for users to visualize hidden meshes, but it would also serve the purpose of helping creators improve their work.\nI'm not so sure about the details as to why the \"Code\" filter was initially remove, but if some filter were to be added and serve as a replacement, I believe this would be a good solution, leaving creators and users satisfied.",
